# Git attributes: https://git-scm.com/docs/gitattributes
# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository and in working trees, on every platform, so
# that hashes, diffs, and the byte-exact test fixtures are identical on Windows, macOS and Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts must keep CRLF to run correctly under cmd.exe.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Lock files are generated: collapse them in diffs and avoid merge-driver line mangling.
Cargo.lock linguist-generated=true -diff
flake.lock linguist-generated=true -diff

# Infinity Engine game resources (see the IESDP file-format reference) must be stored byte-exact,
# so that test fixtures and installed output match the original bytes on every platform. Text-like tables (2DA, IDS) disable normalisation but stay diffable; every other
# resource type is treated as binary (no normalisation, no textual diff or merge).
*.2da -text
*.ids -text
*.bif binary
*.bam binary
*.key binary
*.tlk binary
*.itm binary
*.spl binary
*.cre binary
*.are binary
*.wed binary
*.tis binary
*.mos binary
*.bcs binary
*.bs binary
*.sto binary
*.eff binary
*.pro binary
*.vvc binary
*.wmp binary
*.chu binary
*.dlg binary
*.gam binary
*.sav binary
*.mus binary
*.acm binary
*.wav binary
*.pvrz binary
*.bmp binary
*.png binary
